* netlist snapshot for gain/GBW/PM Monte Carlo record 20261018-200352-119ceb4 (issue #129)
* ---- committed testbench (sim/gain-gbw-pm/testbench/tb_gain_gbw_pm.spice) + mismatch switch ----
* | * tb_gain_gbw_pm.spice -- open-loop AC testbench for the committed sized
* | * schematic (issue #38; spec rows: open-loop DC gain, GBW, phase margin).
* | *
* | * DEVICE UNDER TEST: the committed xschem export
* | * design/netlist/opamp_two_stage.spice, instantiated as `opamp_two_stage`
* | * (ports: vdd vss vinp vinn vout ibias). NO TRANSISTOR IS DECLARED IN THIS
* | * FILE -- every device, including the Miller cap CC and nulling resistor RZ,
* | * comes from the DUT include below. The driver (run_gain_gbw_pm.py)
* | * materialises `opamp_two_stage.dut.spice` from the committed export by the
* | * same wrapper normalisation design/check_dc_op.py uses (uncomment xschem's
* | * `**.subckt`/`**.ends`, drop the deck-terminating `.end`; nothing else is
* | * touched) and rewrites the two `.include` targets below to absolute paths
* | * of the per-run work directory. test_gain_gbw_pm.py guards that both
* | * includes are present and that no transistor is declared here.
* | *
* | * This file is a CIRCUIT BODY in `klt sim`'s sense: no `.lib`, `.temp`,
* | * `.control` or `.end`. `klt sim` adds the corner's `.lib` cards, `.temp`,
* | * the supply `alter`s and the `.ac` analysis.
* | *
* | * ---- Bias and load (design/README.md; spec/target-spec.md Sec.1) ----
* | *   - Ibias: 10 uA driven INTO the `ibias` node from vdd (the polarity
* | *     design/check_dc_op.py uses).
* | *   - CL = 2 pF [DR-1] on vout.
* | *   - Input common mode tracks VDD/2: `Vcm` and `Vdd` are swept together
* | *     by `klt sim` (corners.supply_v keys vdd and vcm move by index).
* | *   - Committed RZ/CC stay in the DUT; this bench neither tunes nor
* | *     bypasses them.
* | *
* | * ---- DC-closed, AC-open arrangement ----
* | * A huge inductor Lfb from vout to the inverting input vinn closes the loop
* | * at DC (unity-gain buffer: the amplifier self-biases at vinn = vout = VCM,
* | * the same operating point design/check_dc_op.py verifies) while being an
* | * AC open: |Z| = 2*pi*f*Lfb >= ~6e8 ohm even at the 0.1 Hz sweep start, far
* | * above the ~Mohm-class output resistance, so it does not load the output
* | * and the loop is open for every swept frequency. A huge capacitor Cfb from
* | * vinn to ground makes vinn an AC ground, so the AC stimulus on vinp is the
* | * whole differential input. The driver still divides by the ACTUAL
* | * differential phasor v(vinp)-v(vinn) rather than assuming it is 1.
* | *
* | * The Lfb/Cfb values are the `.param` line below; the driver rewrites that
* | * line (and only that line) for the feedback-isolation sweep that
* | * demonstrates the measured low-frequency plateau does not depend on the
* | * isolation (see the record). A SMALL Lfb loads the output and shows up as
* | * a spurious gain rise with frequency instead of a plateau -- that is the
* | * failure mode the plateau check exists to catch.
* | *
* | * ---- Polarity ----
* | * vinp is the non-inverting input: the plateau gain must come out
* | * positive-real (phase ~ 0 deg). The driver fails a point whose plateau
* | * phase is not within 10 deg of 0.
* | 
* | .include 'design.ngspice'
* | .param sw_stat_mismatch=1
* | .include 'opamp_two_stage.dut.spice'
* | 
* | .param lfb=1e9 cfb=1e9
* | 
* | Vdd vdd 0 dc 3.3
* | Vcm vinp 0 dc 1.65 ac 1
* | Ibias vdd ibias dc 10u
* | Xdut vdd 0 vinp vinn vout ibias opamp_two_stage
* | Lfb vout vinn {lfb}
* | Cfb vinn 0 {cfb}
* | CL vout 0 2p
